.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt IDEAPAD 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ideapad
.Nd the Lenovo IdeaPad's keys and Wi-Fi switch
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /dev/input/eventN ,
.Dq Ideapad extra buttons
.Pp
.Pa /sys/class/rfkill/rfkillN ,
.Ql ideapad_wlan
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Lenovo's IdeaPad laptops, the G50-70 among them, report some of their keys,
the airplane key among them, through the ACPI device
.Ql VPC2004 ,
under the embedded controller, and not through the keyboard.
The kernel drives the first present
.Ql VPC2004
as Linux's
.Nm ideapad-laptop
does, through the device's methods
.Ql VPCR
and
.Ql VPCW ,
which read and write the controller's command and data registers.
A command is written, the controller clears the command register once it
has taken it, and the data register then holds the answer; a command the
controller has not taken within 200 ms fails.
One command runs at a time.
.Pp
At boot the kernel evaluates the device's
.Ql _CFG
for the machine's radios, registers the event device
.Dq Ideapad extra buttons ,
and turns the controller's radio switch on, so that the controller blocks
no radio of its own accord.
When
.Ql _CFG
says the machine has Wi-Fi, bit 18, it registers the rfkill switch
.Ql ideapad_wlan ,
of type
.Ql wlan ,
which belongs to no radio: its soft block is written to the controller's
Wi-Fi bit, 0 blocking and 1 not, and nothing is written at boot.
.Pp
On each Notify the kernel reads the event bits, the controller's byte
.Ql VPC1
and above it its byte
.Ql VPC2 ,
which the reads clear, and reports the keys of the bits
that are set, each pressed and released at once, as
.Xr acpi 4 Ns 's
other devices report theirs:
.Bl -column "bit 13" "KEY_SWITCHVIDEOMODE" -offset indent
.It bit 6 Ta Dv KEY_SWITCHVIDEOMODE
.It bit 7 Ta Dv KEY_CAMERA
.It bit 8 Ta Dv KEY_MICMUTE
.It bit 11 Ta Dv KEY_F16
.It bit 13 Ta Dv KEY_WLAN , No the airplane key
.El
.Pp
Bit 9 reads the controller's radio switch again.
On the machines with a radio switch of their own, which Linux lists by
name, Linux makes the controller's switch the hard block of
.Ql ideapad_wlan ;
the kernel lists none, so the switch is only logged and no hard block is
set.
The other bits, such as bit 4 of the brightness keys, which the video bus
reports, give no key.
.Pp
.Dv KEY_WLAN
does not change a switch by itself.
.Xr acpid 1
runs
.Pa /etc/acpi/wifi
for it, which blocks every Wi-Fi switch when one has its soft block clear,
and unblocks every one otherwise; see
.Xr init 8 .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/acpi/wifi
.It Pa /etc/acpi.map
.Dv KEY_WLAN
as the event
.Ql button/wlan WLAN
.It Pa /etc/acpi/wifi
the airplane key's action
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
The lines are at the debug level, which the serial port and the log keep
and the screen does not show, but for the warnings.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ql acpi: ideapad: PATH: cfg 0xC, wifi W, ideapad_wlan
The device at PATH was taken; C is what
.Ql _CFG
returned, W the controller's Wi-Fi bit, and
.Ql ideapad_wlan
is there when the switch was registered.
.It Ql acpi: ideapad: radio switch N
The controller's radio switch, 1 when it lets the radios run.
.It Ql acpi: event: ideapad: notify 0xV
A Notify of value V on the device.
.It Ql acpi: event: ideapad: bits 0xB
The events the Notify read.
.It Ql acpi: event: ideapad: bit N: key K
Event bit N reported as key K.
.It Ql acpi: ideapad: read 0xC: error E
The controller did not answer command C, with -110 for a timeout.
.Ql write
is the same of a command that writes.
.It Ql acpi: ideapad: refused: PATH: _CFG: EXCEPTION
The device's
.Ql _CFG
failed, and the device is not taken.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr acpid 1 ,
.Xr acpi 4 ,
.Xr input 4 ,
.Xr rfkill 4 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr rfkill 8
.Sh HISTORY
The driver follows Linux's
.Nm ideapad-laptop .
.Sh BUGS
Which event bit the G50-70's airplane key sets is not yet measured; bit 13
is Linux's, and the controller's queries
.Ql _Q1C
and
.Ql _Q44
are the candidates.
The novo button, the touchpad's switch, the camera's and Bluetooth's
switches and the keyboard's Fn lock are not driven.
